{"published_at": "Tue, 29 Sep 2026 21:43:55 +0000", "summary": "<p><a href=\"https://medcitynews.com/2026/09/unite-us-instacart-link-care-coordination-and-grocery-benefits-to-scale-food-as-medicine/\"><img width=\"600\" height=\"392\" src=\"https://medcitynews.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/7/2021/09/GettyImages-925101084-600x392.jpg\" class=\"attachment-large size-large wp-post-image\" alt=\"\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto!important;\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"https://medcitynews.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/7/2021/09/GettyImages-925101084-600x392.jpg 600w, https://medcitynews.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/7/2021/09/GettyImages-925101084-300x196.jpg 300w, https://medcitynews.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/7/2021/09/GettyImages-925101084.jpg 732w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 600px) 100vw, 600px\" /></a></p><p>Unite Us and Instacart announced Tuesday that they are partnering to connect healthcare organizations’ care coordination efforts with grocery benefits, with the aim of making food-as-medicine programs easier to launch and operate at scale.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://medcitynews.com/2026/09/unite-us-instacart-link-care-coordination-and-grocery-benefits-to-scale-food-as-medicine/\">Unite Us, Instacart Link Care Coordination and Grocery Benefits to Scale Food-as-Medicine</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://medcitynews.com\">MedCity News</a>.</p>\n", "tags": [], "title": "Unite Us, Instacart Link Care Coordination and Grocery Benefits to Scale Food-as-Medicine", "upstream_id": "https://medcitynews.com/?p=150305", "url": "https://medcitynews.com/2026/09/unite-us-instacart-link-care-coordination-and-grocery-benefits-to-scale-food-as-medicine/"}
{"published_at": "Tue, 29 Sep 2026 19:25:15 +0000", "summary": "<p><a href=\"https://medcitynews.com/2026/09/astrazeneca-summit-therapeutics-gastrointestinal-cancer-pd-1-vegf-bispecific-antibody-adc-combination-smmt-azn/\"><img width=\"600\" height=\"400\" src=\"https://medcitynews.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/7/2021/08/GettyImages-1317445583-600x400.jpg\" class=\"attachment-large size-large wp-post-image\" alt=\"\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto!important;\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"https://medcitynews.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/7/2021/08/GettyImages-1317445583-600x400.jpg 600w, https://medcitynews.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/7/2021/08/GettyImages-1317445583-300x200.jpg 300w, https://medcitynews.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/7/2021/08/GettyImages-1317445583-768x512.jpg 768w, https://medcitynews.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/7/2021/08/GettyImages-1317445583.jpg 1024w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 600px) 100vw, 600px\" /></a></p><p>AstraZeneca’s equity investment in Summit Therapeutics comes with plans for clinical trial collaborations. The deal brings AstraZeneca into a growing group of pharmaceutical companies testing the pairing of antibody drug conjugates with PD-1/VEGF bispecific antibodies, a drug combination that could offer advantages in cancer treatment.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://medcitynews.com/2026/09/astrazeneca-summit-therapeutics-gastrointestinal-cancer-pd-1-vegf-bispecific-antibody-adc-combination-smmt-azn/\">AstraZeneca Places a $2B Bet on a Summit Therapeutics Cancer Drug</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://medcitynews.com\">MedCity News</a>.</p>\n", "tags": [], "title": "AstraZeneca Places a $2B Bet on a Summit Therapeutics Cancer Drug", "upstream_id": "https://medcitynews.com/?p=150298", "url": "https://medcitynews.com/2026/09/astrazeneca-summit-therapeutics-gastrointestinal-cancer-pd-1-vegf-bispecific-antibody-adc-combination-smmt-azn/"}
{"published_at": "Tue, 29 Sep 2026 18:13:41 +0000", "summary": "<p><a href=\"https://medcitynews.com/2026/09/medcity-pivot-podcast-a-conversation-with-alivecors-priya-abani/\"><img width=\"1024\" height=\"576\" src=\"https://medcitynews.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/7/2026/09/MP084-WIDE1-1024x576.jpg\" class=\"attachment-large size-large wp-post-image\" alt=\"\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto!important;\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"https://medcitynews.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/7/2026/09/MP084-WIDE1-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://medcitynews.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/7/2026/09/MP084-WIDE1-300x169.jpg 300w, https://medcitynews.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/7/2026/09/MP084-WIDE1-768x432.jpg 768w, https://medcitynews.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/7/2026/09/MP084-WIDE1-1536x864.jpg 1536w, https://medcitynews.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/7/2026/09/MP084-WIDE1.jpg 1920w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" /></a></p><p>In this episode of the MedCity Pivot Podcast, CEO Priya Abani talks about the evolution of AliveCor, one of the earliest digital health companies. </p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://medcitynews.com/2026/09/medcity-pivot-podcast-a-conversation-with-alivecors-priya-abani/\">MedCity Pivot Podcast: A Conversation With AliveCor&#8217;s Priya Abani</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://medcitynews.com\">MedCity News</a>.</p>\n", "tags": [], "title": "MedCity Pivot Podcast: A Conversation With AliveCor’s Priya Abani", "upstream_id": "https://medcitynews.com/?p=150289", "url": "https://medcitynews.com/2026/09/medcity-pivot-podcast-a-conversation-with-alivecors-priya-abani/"}
{"published_at": "Tue, 29 Sep 2026 09:52:38 +0000", "summary": "<p><a href=\"https://medcitynews.com/2026/09/the-illegal-drug-marketplace-in-your-patients-pockets/\"><img width=\"600\" height=\"558\" src=\"https://medcitynews.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/7/2016/08/talk-bubble-600x558.jpg\" class=\"attachment-large size-large wp-post-image\" alt=\"\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto!important;\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"https://medcitynews.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/7/2016/08/talk-bubble-600x558.jpg 600w, https://medcitynews.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/7/2016/08/talk-bubble-300x279.jpg 300w, https://medcitynews.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/7/2016/08/talk-bubble.jpg 613w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 600px) 100vw, 600px\" /></a></p><p>Patients obtaining drugs through social media, medical spas, or telehealth platforms are not the same as patients obtaining drugs through more traditional illicit channels because they often believe what they are receiving is a clinically validated product. This means they may present with unexplained symptoms without realizing their online purchase is even relevant to the conversation</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://medcitynews.com/2026/09/the-illegal-drug-marketplace-in-your-patients-pockets/\">The Illegal Drug Marketplace in Your Patients’ Pockets</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://medcitynews.com\">MedCity News</a>.</p>\n", "tags": [], "title": "The Illegal Drug Marketplace in Your Patients’ Pockets", "upstream_id": "https://medcitynews.com/?p=149930", "url": "https://medcitynews.com/2026/09/the-illegal-drug-marketplace-in-your-patients-pockets/"}
{"published_at": "Mon, 28 Sep 2026 23:12:46 +0000", "summary": "<p><a href=\"https://medcitynews.com/2026/09/dreamed-wins-fda-clearance-for-cgm-driven-insulin-automation-tool-for-both-type-2-injection-regimens/\"><img width=\"600\" height=\"400\" src=\"https://medcitynews.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/7/2020/01/GettyImages-869846050-600x400.jpg\" class=\"attachment-large size-large wp-post-image\" alt=\"\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto!important;\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"https://medcitynews.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/7/2020/01/GettyImages-869846050-600x400.jpg 600w, https://medcitynews.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/7/2020/01/GettyImages-869846050-300x200.jpg 300w, https://medcitynews.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/7/2020/01/GettyImages-869846050.jpg 724w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 600px) 100vw, 600px\" /></a></p><p>DreaMed Diabetes has received FDA 510(K) clearance for MODI, a mobile app that uses CGM (continuous glucose monitoring) data to provide insulin dosing recommendations for people with Type 2 diabetes who need both basal insulin and fast-acting injections. </p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://medcitynews.com/2026/09/dreamed-wins-fda-clearance-for-cgm-driven-insulin-automation-tool-for-both-type-2-injection-regimens/\">DreaMed Wins FDA Clearance for CGM-Driven Insulin Automation Tool for Both Type 2 Injection Regimens</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://medcitynews.com\">MedCity News</a>.</p>\n", "tags": [], "title": "DreaMed Wins FDA Clearance for CGM-Driven Insulin Automation Tool for Both Type 2 Injection Regimens", "upstream_id": "https://medcitynews.com/?p=150271", "url": "https://medcitynews.com/2026/09/dreamed-wins-fda-clearance-for-cgm-driven-insulin-automation-tool-for-both-type-2-injection-regimens/"}
